	(text "THE KEYBOARD ON THE BUS: KEY LATCH (7802), STATUS (7804), KEY-READY, THE FLAG LINE" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "deb37d6e-33db-5ca4-9519-b0f9a58bcda2"))
	(text "IC16: -RDKEY and -RDSTAT are the decoder's selects while -MRD is low; KRDT is -RDKEY while TPB is high. IC19, the key latch,\ndrives D0-D7 while -RDKEY is low; IC20 puts the status on them while -RDSTAT is low: bit 0 KEY-READY, 2 VSYNC, 3 DE, 7 = 1.\nThe ATmega's LDDATA edge loads IC19 and sets KEY-READY (IC18B); KCLR (IC17: KRDT, or -RESET) clears it: a read of the key,\nat TPB. IC18A is the 6845's E: -CLR on ground, -MRW on -PRE: Q = NOT -MRW. IC22 (7416, open collector) pulls the bus flag line JP1 picks (-EF1, -EF2, -EF3 or -EF) low while KEY-READY, and\nthe ATmega's reset (MRST) low while RESETH; R11 pulls -EF up." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8adf9306-00e2-5cf7-95b6-c55c880a54ef"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
